# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere.
#
# Development happens on Windows; everything runs in Linux containers. CRLF
# surviving into an image produces failures that read as anything but a line
# ending problem: shell scripts die with "bad interpreter: no such file or
# directory", and cron silently ignores the offending line.
#
# Storing and checking out LF avoids the whole category.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where CRLF is fatal rather than untidy.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
crontab     text eol=lf

# Generated by uv. Collapse it in diffs and exclude it from language stats.
uv.lock linguist-generated=true
